### 3. Three critical corrections to the local agent's interpretation

First, don't conflate simulation agreement with validation. C1's 0.1–0.2% WAPE establishes an excellent approximation to W2-Air under the tested assumptions. It does not establish accuracy against measured facility water.

Second, the Step 30 result is important but limited. C1 and W2 achieve the same reference-optimal evaporation, with zero conditional regret. That does not necessarily prove identical hourly schedules, since multiple optimal solutions can exist. More importantly, the 2.6% reduction in modeled daily evaporation comes with a 7.3% increase in peak treatment feed.

Third, the Prineville near-reconciliation is not independent validation. The 179.8 ML versus 180 ML agreement is promising, but the city and Meta figures may share underlying measurements. A figure emphasizing the 0.13% difference could give it more evidential weight than warranted.

